      "body": "## Summary\n\n#8840 copies each pinned CPU master partition to the device in float32 and casts it there. It moves the whole sub-group at once, so with `offload_optimizer.pin_memory: true` (the default) `step()` needs a float32 device temporary of a whole sub-group: up to 3.73 GiB at the default `sub_group_size` of 1e9. The description of #8840 says the copy goes in pieces of 2**26 elements (0.25 GiB); the merged code does not. No release has #8840 yet.\n\nThis PR copies in pieces of 2**26 elements, in order on one stream, so each piece reuses the memory of the previous one. ZeRO-1/2 cast on the host into a pinned 16-bit buffer and have no device temporary; SuperOffload and ZenFlow's overlap step copy the masters their own way.\n\nNo open issue or PR covers this.\n\n## Fixes\n\nBefore → after, 1 GH200, bf16, ZeRO-3 with `offload_optimizer: {device: cpu, pin_memory: true}`, base `1a956270f`. Device memory that `step()` takes on top of what is allocated before it:\n\n1. 1.0B parameters, default `sub_group_size` (one sub-group of 1007M elements): 3.75 → 0.25 GiB.\n2. 134M parameters: 0.50 → 0.25 GiB.\n\nThe step time does not change (1.0B: 0.178 → 0.178 s; copy-back 12.7 → 12.8 ms).\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
